{"name":"Cherry Crush","hex":"#c71414","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cherry","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small fruit, usually red, black or yellow, with a smooth hard seed and a short hard stem.","Prunus subg. Cerasus, trees or shrubs that bear cherries."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Containing or having the taste of cherries.","Of a bright red color; cherry red."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cherry"},{"term":"crush","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A violent collision or compression; a crash; destruction; ruin.","Violent pressure, as of a moving crowd."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To press between two hard objects; to squeeze so as to alter the natural shape or integrity, or to force together into a mass.","To reduce to fine particles by pounding or grinding."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crush"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cherry Crush","blocks":[{"text":"Cherry Crush is a 2007 American drama thriller film directed and co-written by Nicholas DiBella. It premiered in Rochester, New York on February 16, 2007 and was released on DVD on July 3, 2007."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/36/Cherrycrush.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cherry_Crush","wikidata":"Q5092336"},{"title":"Cherry Crush (novel)","blocks":[{"text":"Cherry Crush is a British novel written by the English author Cathy Cassidy. It is the first book in the Chocolate Box Girls series. The book revolves around the suddenly upturned life of Cherry Costello who just moved to Somerset with her father to live with her father's girlfriend Charlotte Tanberry. When she arrives there, she realizes she has four new sisters. The plot deals with her attraction to her new stepsister's boyfriend Shay, while maintaining her desire to fit in."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/13/Cherry_crush.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cherry_Crush_(novel)","wikidata":"Q5092333"},{"title":"Cherry","blocks":[{"text":"A cherry is the fruit of many plants of the genus Prunus, and is a fleshy drupe."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Cherry_season_%2848216568227%29.jpg/330px-Cherry_season_%2848216568227%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cherry","wikidata":"Q196"},{"title":"Cerise (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Cerise is a dark pink shade."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Bandyball1.jpg/330px-Bandyball1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cerise_(color)","wikidata":"Q2334511"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Italienische_S%C3%BC%C3%9Fkirschen.JPG/500px-Italienische_S%C3%BC%C3%9Fkirschen.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Italienische_S%C3%BC%C3%9Fkirschen.JPG/1280px-Italienische_S%C3%BC%C3%9Fkirschen.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Italienische_S%C3%BC%C3%9Fkirschen.JPG/500px-Italienische_S%C3%BC%C3%9Fkirschen.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Prunus avium, sweet cherry","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AItalienische_S%C3%BC%C3%9Fkirschen.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/Sara_Ploos_van_Amstel_-_The_Cherry_Seller_-_watercolor_after_Jacob_Ochtervelt.jpg/500px-Sara_Ploos_van_Amstel_-_The_Cherry_Seller_-_watercolor_after_Jacob_Ochtervelt.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, ht